{
  "description": "Guard matrix of the local dashboard server shared by the Python and TypeScript shells. Each case builds the fake world, signs in (session signed) or not (anonymous), substitutes {port}, {host}, {cookieName}, {csrf} and {startTarget} in the request and calls LocalApp.respond with lower-cased headers. A header with a null value is removed. expect: status; errorCode of the JSON error; headers (a null value means the header is absent from the reply); setCookieHas/setCookieLacks (attributes of Set-Cookie); bodyHas (keys of the JSON body), bodyText, bodyContains, contentTypePrefix; writes, noPlaneCalls and costQueries as in api-v1-cases.json. redeemFirst burns the start token before the request.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "without the session cookie / answers 401",
      "world": {},
      "session": "anonymous",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "target": "/",
        "headers": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 401,
        "errorCode": "unauthorized"
      }
    },
